## Shared contract

```xml
<shared_contract>

<labelling>
Deny by default. Every emitted interpretive claim carries one of VERIFIED,
TRADITIONAL or UNVERIFIED, drawn from the same registry the /accuracy page
renders. A claim with no label is a bug. UNVERIFIED.md must stay in parity with
that registry — assert it, never eyeball it.
</labelling>

<basis>
Classical citations are mandatory in code comments: BPHS chapter and verse,
Prashna Marga chapter, Phaladeepika verse. A rule with no citation is TRADITIONAL
at best and must be labelled so.
</basis>

<determinism>
as_of from answerCardAsOf.ts, never the clock. No LLM in a card path. No
Math.random. answers:check is a real gate; a byte-unstable card is a bug.
</determinism>

<confidentiality>
Seed-bank birth data is private. Nothing in public/ may carry dob, tob, place,
lat, lon, tz. Redaction flows through redact.ts only. assertNoPii() must pass on
every write. A client check is UX, not authz.
</confidentiality>

<inherited_invariants>
Folders persist when empty. TypeScript strict, zero new any, no new @ts-nocheck.
Bilingual { en, hi } on every user-visible string, Hindi in Devanagari. Edge
functions use relative .ts imports. SPDX header on every new file. Conventional
commits with DCO sign-off: Signed-off-by: RAJKUMAR SINGH CHAUHAN <crajkumarsingh@hotmail.com>
CREAT.MD appended at top, pruned past 24h, refreshed at least every 12 minutes.
</inherited_invariants>

<gates>
Stop at the first red. Paste raw output.

  npx tsc --noEmit
  npm run lint
  npm run test:run
  npm run typecheck:edge
  npm run test:accuracy:corpus
  npm run test:accuracy:varga
  npm run test:tz-wiring
  npm run answers:emit && npm run answers:check
  npm run docs:verify
  npm run build

Add per-domain gates where the block names them.
</gates>

<approval>
Ask before: pushing, opening a PR, writing public/answers/**, adding a
dependency, touching corpus or golden files, changing a pinned count, deleting a
referenced file, raising a perf baseline.

Never: commit to main, force-push, rewrite history, amend a pushed commit,
migrate production, print secrets. Read .env.example and name the var.

Halt and ask when a gate is red for an unrelated reason, a citation and an
existing test disagree, redaction trips, or a block needs a type that does not
exist.
</approval>

<output>
Branch per block, PR body with: claim labels touched, evidence table
(gate | command | exit | tail), redaction grep result, risk note, CREAT.MD text.
End with START HERE FIRST — then the highest-blast-radius open item.
</output>

</shared_contract>
```

